(7696588, 1261799, 87808, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> Hilarious! ...is it actually the same bird? (the absence of shadow off the right owl triggered my suspicion).<br/>ETA: I take it back, I think there is a shadow from bird 3, just not very obvious) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Weirdly enough, I agree with you about the shadows. All three of them should have shadows. How he does not have a shadow, I don''t know. I think it sort of fell behind him. It was pretty uneven ground and I cropped to make the ground straight versus the concrete bank and I was also shooting downwards.  Behind his back leg, there is a faint backwards shadow going towards the dip of the bank.  It''s a great but odd optical illusion!</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: Hilarious! ...is it actually the same bird? (the absence of shadow off the right owl triggered my suspicion).ETA: I take it back, I think there is a shadow from bird 3, just not very obvious)   Weirdly enough, I agree with you about the shadows. All three of them should have shadows. How he does not have a shadow, I don''t know. I think it sort of fell behind him. It was pretty uneven ground and I cropped to make the ground straight versus the concrete bank and I was also shooting downwards.  Behind his back leg, there is a faint backwards shadow going towards the dip of the bank.  It''s a great but odd optical illusion!', '2021-06-26 09:27:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7696661, 1262225, 273092, '<td valign="top">These things really look amazing</td>', 'These things really look amazing', '2021-06-27 14:49:39.000000', NULL, 0),
